{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"7685867e5c75de0355fe342e77a7207124eae0e79d80edf5701afb146987ce99","packTokens":2266,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":162,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1331,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":666,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"The product stories describe behaviors beyond the locked API contract, while the final instruction says to implement the contract exactly. When a story requires behavior the contract does not define, which scope should govern?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only operations and behavior defined by the locked OpenAPI contract; do not add uncontracted behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For sample rows that refer to one another, should the seeder create compatible references, or may it seed each table independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create compatible references between related sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"The contract includes an operation to return a configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, but the provider and source of that configuration are not identified here. What should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider and supply its authorization URL and token-validation settings through deployment configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When demo seeding is disabled and a database table has no records, should list operations return an empty list or provide sample rows without persisting them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return an empty list when the database has no matching records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The staff identity-provider URL and token-validation settings will come from deployment configuration. What should happen if required settings are missing or invalid?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail application startup with a clear configuration error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Apply a reviewed database migration during deployment, preserving existing data; use EnsureCreated only for genuinely empty databases.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should schema changes be applied to databases that already exist when the new persistent tables are introduced?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Have deployment provision the initial account outside the API; do not add an API bootstrap flow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With demo seeding disabled, how should the first PostgreSQL account be made available so the API can authorize callers?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Identify the organization's existing staff provider and supply its authorization URL and validation settings; do not introduce a new provider.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which staff identity provider and concrete authorization-URL and token-validation settings should the API use?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Provide valid nonproduction settings for the chosen provider through test and factory configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the test and factory runs obtain the valid nonproduction identity-provider settings required for startup?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Keep behavior limited to the locked contract; use standard secure password hashing for stored passwords, and do not add new lockout or one-time-code policies.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How much customer-authentication behavior beyond the locked contract should be specified for failed logins and password storage?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Match the token's email claim to the account email, and deny access when no matching enabled account exists.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Which token claim should identify the PostgreSQL staff account, and what should happen if a valid token has no matching or has a disabled account?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"For a stock collection request whose filter names a warehouse outside the caller’s scope, what should the API return?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return 200 OK with an empty list, applying the caller’s scope to the results.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authorization include a separate role-to-operation permission table beyond the roles and scopes stated in the locked contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not add a separate role-to-operation table; enforce only the role and scope restrictions stated by the locked contract.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"How should startup determine whether a database qualifies for EnsureCreated, given that existing databases must use the reviewed deployment migration?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use EnsureCreated only when the database has no tables; otherwise leave schema changes to the reviewed deployment migration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement only the operations and behavior defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, retaining the root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes; ensure responses, filtering, and scope enforcement conform to the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist contract-operation business changes to the configured PostgreSQL database; apply only contract-defined lifecycle constraints, use `EnsureCreated` only when the database has no tables, and leave schema changes to reviewed migrations that preserve existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Run `SeedData.Run` at startup when `Seed:Demo` is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Make `SeedData.Run` add two to five contract-example-based rows only to each empty contract-backed table, preserve existing rows, and create references to existing related rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is false or unset, do not run the demo seeder or create demo rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Return an empty list, not unpersisted sample records, when a contract collection operation has no matching persisted records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Use the organization's existing staff identity provider, obtain its authorization URL and token-validation settings from deployment configuration, and use valid nonproduction settings in test and factory configurations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Fail application startup with an error identifying the affected setting when a required staff identity-provider authorization URL or token-validation setting is missing or invalid; keep the existing health test and factory checks able to reach the health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes with valid nonproduction settings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer and staff authentication and authorization only through the locked contract; store customer passwords using a standard salted password hash; authorize only by contract-stated roles and scopes, without a separate role-to-operation permission table; match staff token email claims to enabled account emails; deny unmatched or disabled accounts; and add no lockout or one-time-code policies beyond the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provision the initial PostgreSQL account through deployment, outside the API, rather than through an API bootstrap flow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}